        <item>
            <title>0.2.1</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:55:31 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>5</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[- A short introduction the first time you run Intention: four screens on what it's for, ending at
  your first intention. It appears only when there's no history to show — a fresh install, or after
  clearing your data — so it never gets in the way of anyone already using the app.

- A new Dashboard section in Settings, for people with a licence, with one thing in it: clear all
  recorded data and start the dashboard again from empty. It says how many sessions it's about to
  delete before you press it, and asks once more after. Your settings and your licence are kept.

- The menu bar item can be trimmed down, under Settings › Personalization › Menu bar item. The
  countdown can be turned off, leaving the menu bar naming what you're working on without a clock
  ticking beside it — useful if a timer in the corner of the screen is the thing you end up watching
  instead of the work. The icon can be turned off too, for a crowded menu bar. Either way the session
  is untouched and still ends at the same time.
]]></description>
